{
	title: 'Safe browser diagnostics and live transcript event isolation',
	spec: 'Browser and terminal transcripts only end a live turn on an explicit turn-end or non-command question event; unrelated session events (including notices and upload acknowledgements) leave the live turn and its items unchanged and cannot create a turn-end with missing status. The Home Screen web client initializes diagnostics before rendering, records bounded structural breadcrumbs for host event types, connection changes, visibility/resume, and tab pointer/click interactions, and reports uncaught JS errors and unhandled promise rejections. Reports contain code version, a per-page random correlation ID, timestamps, structural view/connection/viewport state and JavaScript error name/location only: no prompt/transcript/draft text, tool inputs/results, arbitrary error messages, URLs, cookies, authentication codes or device identity. The tab menu has a Send diagnostics action. Reports reach the host over a cookie-authenticated same-origin POST endpoint independently of the WebSocket, are validated and byte/rate bounded, and go to owner-only rotating state/web-diag.log (one 1 MiB file plus one previous file), never conversation history or tracked files. Diagnostics are best effort, must never break interactions, and use bounded memory without persistent browser storage. Tests cover unrelated live events, auth/origin/body validation, privacy filtering and bounded logging. Diagnostics do not claim to establish the historical cause of a frozen page without captured evidence. Browser controller callbacks defer circular module references until invocation so browser modules can be imported safely in any order.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'The phantom end was caused by live transcript.fold falling through on attached (or another non-transcript session event), not a missing status sent by the host. Guard the ending branch, rather than hide the undefined label; the next stream must still append to the same live block. The app/tabs cycle also had an eager tabs.backgroundStep reference; a lazy callback fixes import-order failures.',
		'Reports are structural and project away unknown fields on the host. Actual body reads are capped at 16 KiB, 32 breadcrumbs per report, 30 accepted attempts per host minute, and client sends at most every five seconds; failed sends retain only the latest 32 entries for a future interaction/resume. Real Chromium mobile smoke exercised tab navigation, manual reporting, uncaught TypeError and rejected RangeError while ensuring their private messages never reached the log. A browser whose main thread is entirely blocked cannot report until it resumes; telemetry is evidence, not proof all freezes are fixed.'
	],
	needs: ['w5', '8a']
}
